{"id": "g2_count_covered_integer_points", "signature": "solve(spans)", "statement": "`spans` is a list of [start, end] pairs of integers with start <= end, each describing a CLOSED range that contains every integer from start to end inclusive. Return the number of distinct integers that are covered by at least one span. Spans may overlap, touch, repeat, or appear in any order, and the input list must not be modified. Return 0 for an empty list.", "tests": [{"args": [[]], "expected": 0}, {"args": [[[1, 2], [2, 3]]], "expected": 3}, {"args": [[[1, 2], [4, 5]]], "expected": 4}, {"args": [[[5, 5]]], "expected": 1}, {"args": [[[1, 10], [3, 4], [7, 8]]], "expected": 10}, {"args": [[[-3, 0], [0, 2]]], "expected": 6}, {"args": [[[2, 2], [2, 2], [2, 2]]], "expected": 1}, {"args": [[[0, 4], [6, 9], [3, 6]]], "expected": 10}, {"args": [[[100, 102], [101, 105]]], "expected": 6}, {"args": [[[-1000, 1000]]], "expected": 2001}, {"args": [[[1, 3], [7, 9]]], "expected": 6}, {"args": [[[4, 6], [1, 2], [3, 3]]], "expected": 6}], "facts": [["arg", "spans", "interval_list"], ["iterate", "spans"], ["ask", "merge_intervals"], ["interval_ends", "closed"], ["interval_output", "covered_count"], ["size", "spans", "tiny"]], "deps": {"schema": ["interval_scan"], "uses": ["interval_merge"], "solution_sha256": "70f5abe4b30ac7b99b411c66868fe6c852d4bef40fa5de7e1c9b8f616ffd7c39", "reference_sha256": "45386d94d5072cdb5e2bf8e26b012a4e5fc888099ac6896762f030a4ecc06aa1"}}